  "summary": "Gateway profile for the Veris H8036: 27 Analog Inputs, all polled. It reads energy consumption, demand, reactive and apparent power, PF total and per phase, line-line and line-neutral voltages, phase currents and average/minimum/maximum demand.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet IP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": true,
  "notes": [
    "Built from Contemporary Controls' BASgatewayLX Modbus device profile Veris_H8036_LX_a.csv; the profile maps the registers in the maker's Modbus register document (https://www.ccontrols.com/support/dp/8035-6MB_implementation.pdf).",
    "Object instances are the ones this profile assigns when it is loaded into the gateway. A site that edited or rebuilt the profile may use different instances.",
    "All 27 rows are flagged for polling in the profile, so every object is served to BACnet once the profile is loaded.",
    "The CSV has no read/write column: Analog/Binary Inputs are read-only and Analog/Binary Outputs are commandable (priority array), which is how the gateway maps them (access inferred). Descriptions give the Modbus register each object reads."
  ],
